From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:19:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: pm8916_wdt: support nowayout

Most watchdog drivers let CONFIG_WATCHDOG_NOWAYOUT, or a nowayout module
parameter, keep userspace from stopping the watchdog once it runs. This
one doesn't, so a watchdog daemon that disarms it on its way out turns it
off whatever the system wants.

systemd does that: systemd-shutdown disarms the watchdog right before it
calls reboot(), so on a comma four a driver whose .shutdown() hangs on the
way down was never reset. With nowayout the watchdog keeps counting
through the kernel's shutdown, and the driver still stops it itself where
nothing will ping it any more (power off, halt, a restart into the
bootloader or a download mode).

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c
index a3b6f696bb..88ea1cf2ea 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/pm8916_wdt.c
@@ -59,6 +59,11 @@ static const struct pm8916_wdt_data pm8998_wdt_data = {
 	.otst3 = BIT(15),
 };
 
+static bool nowayout = WATCHDOG_NOWAYOUT;
+module_param(nowayout, bool, 0);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(nowayout, "Watchdog cannot be stopped once started (default="
+		 __MODULE_STRING(WATCHDOG_NOWAYOUT) ")");
+
 struct pm8916_wdt {
 	struct regmap *regmap;
 	struct watchdog_device wdev;
@@ -297,6 +302,7 @@ static int pm8916_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	wdt->wdev.max_timeout = PM8916_WDT_MAX_TIMEOUT;
 	wdt->wdev.timeout = PM8916_WDT_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT;
 	wdt->wdev.pretimeout = 0;
+	watchdog_set_nowayout(&wdt->wdev, nowayout);
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&wdt->wdev, wdt);
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, wdt);
 
